WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.596
A night train heading north. A Thursday
afternoon flight. A climb to Abha.

00:00:05.663 --> 00:00:07.705
A student going home to Tabuk.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:14.331
Jeddah–Riyadh in 2025: about 9.8 million
scheduled air seats,

00:00:14.399 --> 00:00:16.298
fifth in OAG's top ten.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.974
Taif, Tabuk, Abha, Najran, Jazan: none

00:00:21.042 --> 00:00:24.991
has a passenger station within 10
kilometres.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.741
A country of 35.3 million people by
mid-2024, and growing.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:37.638
On Riyadh–Jeddah, air stays ahead door to
door in every rail case.

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:42.983
Every line routed over real terrain,
priced from a register,

00:00:43.051 --> 00:00:46.045
with the overruns big rail projects have
had.

00:00:47.433 --> 00:00:52.263
One frozen judge. 10,000 draws. A record
of every attempt.

00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:58.948
The three-station central case stays
positive even at high cost:

00:00:59.016 --> 00:01:01.933
between 4.0 and 5.6 billion riyals.

00:01:03.333 --> 00:01:07.605
No option pays for itself. The state pays
under every delivery model.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.365
A railway that connects the country is a
possibility, not a promise.

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:16.810
A Railway to Connect the Country.
